      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "National level",
      "pageStart": 25,
      "pageEnd": 25,
      "target": "../sections/sec-020-national-level.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "■The recommendations in the 2017 guidelines on advanced HIV disease (5) (and other related \nupdated WHO guidelines) need to be adopted in national policy and guidelines.\n\t\n■It is important to try to align recommendations across multiple guidelines relating not only \nto HIV (for example, TB and HIV guidelines relating to TB preventive treatment) but also to \nroutine child health and development interventions (vitamin A, deworming and Expanded \nProgramme on Immunization).\n\t\n■Registration and procurement of the required commodities and medication (especially \nformulations for children) are vital",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists national-level implementation steps, such as adopting the guidelines, aligning HIV, TB and child health guidance, procuring child formulations and enabling catch-up vaccination.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
