    {
      "id": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-021",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Facility level",
      "pageStart": 25,
      "pageEnd": 26,
      "target": "../sections/sec-021-facility-level.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "■Currently, the advanced HIV disease package is being implemented as a hub-and-spoke model. \nFurther guidance on this is available in the global advanced HIV disease toolkit (http://www.\ndifferentiatedcare.org/Resources/Resource-Library/Global-Advanced-HIV-DiseaseToolkit).\n\t\n■In the context of ongoing and enhanced efforts to ensure task shifting for services for children, \nall cadres of health-care workers need training for certain components of the package such as \nscreening and enhanced antiretroviral therapy counselling.\n\t\n■Centres introducing the advanced HIV disease package for children s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists facility-level considerations for the paediatric advanced HIV disease package, including hub-and-spoke delivery, task shifting, child-friendly settings and equipment. It also stresses functioning referral systems, for example for safe administration of amphotericin B.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
