      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Health-care providers",
      "pageStart": 26,
      "pageEnd": 26,
      "target": "../sections/sec-022-health-care-providers.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "■Health-care providers should be sensitized on child-specific issues such as growth monitoring \nand other routine child health interventions.\n\t\n■Training and capacity building for staff should be implemented in sites where these \nrecommendations are to be implemented.\n\t\n■Ensure that the advanced HIV disease package is included in any curriculum of training on HIV \nrelated to children or adolescents.\n\t\n■Uptake of TB screening specific to children is challenging. Ensure appropriate adaptation of \nexisting screening tools for the advanced HIV disease package that focus on the different ways \nthat",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists actions for health-care providers, such as training on child health issues and paediatric TB screening, and stresses that clinical diagnosis and treatment of TB should continue when tests are unavailable or negative.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
