      "title": "Laboratory",
      "pageStart": 26,
      "pageEnd": 26,
      "target": "../sections/sec-023-laboratory.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "■Ensure that protocols and standard operating procedures are in place for obtaining and \ntransporting specimens from young children. Training and expertise in paediatric phlebotomy \nand ordering urine bags, gastric washings, sputum induction and stool collection and \nprocessing need to be considered.\n\t\n■Explore the capacity for antibiotic resistance surveillance to ensure that the optimal first-line \ntreatment for severe bacterial infections is being used.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Calls for laboratory procedures for collecting specimens from young children and for antibiotic resistance surveillance.",
