      "target": "../sections/sec-024-monitoring-and-evaluation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "■Monitor the potential toxicity of children receiving TB preventive treatment, co-trimoxazole \nplus antiretroviral therapy (and potentially fluconazole for adolescents).\n\t\n■Monitoring tools need to be developed for the advanced HIV disease package that are specific \nto children.\nTable 4. Cost implications and considerations for commodities\nMedicines (dosage form and pack size)\nReference price excluding \ntransport (USD)\nSourcea\nTB and co-trimoxazole preventive therapy in HIV\nIsoniazid, 300-mg tablet, 30\n0.75\nGlobal Fund Pooled Procurement Mechanism\nIsoniazid, 100-mg tablet, 100b\n1.29\nGlobal Fun",
      "truncated": true,
